  "text": {
    "TXT_KEY_TECH_CARD_RITE_OF_THE_NECROPOLIS": "Rite of the Necropolis",
    "TXT_KEY_TECH_CARD_RITE_OF_THE_NECROPOLIS_HELP": "[ICON_BULLET]World spell, once: the Necropolis is born on the three City Ruins nearest your capital: three cities of size 2, each with Walls and two Pyre Zombies.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Its hero: the Lich-Prince (magic 70, Death Grip in battle, Immortal).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Its cities need no food (Fallow).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Each living unit killed in a battle on its land rises there as its Pyre Zombie.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]+4 attitude toward you, -4 toward good civilizations.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Needs three City Ruins a city can stand on (unowned or yours) and a free player slot.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Not drawn by good civilizations.",
    "TXT_KEY_TECH_CARD_RITE_OF_THE_NECROPOLIS_PEDIA": "The old dead of the fallen cities do not lie quiet. Speak the rite over their ruins and they build again, in bone.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE]Expert: raise it on the ruins your rivals must march past, never beside your own expansion.",
    "TXT_KEY_SPELL_RITE_OF_THE_NECROPOLIS": "Rite of the Necropolis",
    "TXT_KEY_SPELL_RITE_OF_THE_NECROPOLIS_HELP": "[ICON_BULLET]The Necropolis is born on the three City Ruins nearest your capital: three cities of size 2, each with Walls and two Pyre Zombies, and the Lich-Prince.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]+4 attitude toward you, -4 toward good civilizations.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Once per game. Needs three City Ruins a city can stand on (unowned or yours) and a free player slot.",
    "TXT_KEY_BUILDING_PALACE_NECROPOLIS": "Palace",
    "TXT_KEY_UNIT_LICH_PRINCE": "Lich-Prince",
    "TXT_KEY_UNIT_LICH_PRINCE_PEDIA": "The Lich-Prince was a king once. He keeps the crown, and the court, and nothing else of that life.",
    "TXT_KEY_UNIT_LICH_PRINCE_STRATEGY": "A Lich far above its era: magic 70 and Death Grip in battle. Immortal: once, killed, it returns to its capital.",
    "TXT_KEY_CIV_NECROPOLIS_DESC": "The Necropolis",
    "TXT_KEY_CIV_NECROPOLIS_SHORT_DESC": "Necropolis",
    "TXT_KEY_CIV_NECROPOLIS_ADJECTIVE": "Necropolitan",
    "TXT_KEY_CIV_NECROPOLIS_HELP": "[ICON_BULLET]Its cities need no food (Fallow).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Each living unit killed in a battle on its land rises there as its Pyre Zombie.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Its Axeman is the Pyre Zombie.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]-4 attitude toward good civilizations.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Hero: the Lich-Prince.",
    "TXT_KEY_CIV_NECROPOLIS_PEDIA": "The Necropolis is a realm of the dead built on the ruins of the living: walled cities of bone where nothing grows and nothing needs to.",
    "TXT_KEY_CITY_NECROPOLIS_1": "Mourncrypt",
    "TXT_KEY_CITY_NECROPOLIS_2": "Ossuary",
    "TXT_KEY_CITY_NECROPOLIS_3": "Grimhold",
    "TXT_KEY_CITY_NECROPOLIS_4": "Pale Gate",
    "TXT_KEY_CITY_NECROPOLIS_5": "Duskbarrow",
    "TXT_KEY_CITY_NECROPOLIS_6": "Sepulchre",
    "TXT_KEY_CITY_NECROPOLIS_7": "Ashcairn",
    "TXT_KEY_CITY_NECROPOLIS_8": "Gravemoor",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_LICH_PRINCE": "The Lich-Prince",
    "TXT_KEY_LEADER_LICH_PRINCE_PEDIA": "Nobody living remembers the Lich-Prince's name, and he has stopped using it. He counts his subjects by the dead, and the count only rises."
  }
}
